# Planner consumer #1 — bare-param mutation inside an `unsafe:` block (a
# straight-line scope: single predecessor, entry hoist dominates). `unsafe` is
# OUT of the ggdef phase-0 subset (elaboration rejects it), so this fixture lives
# in known_gaps/ (not corpus-harvested / not ggdef-adjudicated) and is validated
# on the two production backends only: C=3,4 and LLVM=3,4 (pre-fix both printed
# 4,4). The Rust `lower_block_scoped` save/restore reverted the in-body rebind;
# the dispatch-arm hoist fixes it. SH note: the SH lowerer has no `unsafe`
# dispatch arm (out of the self-host subset) — construct-unimplemented, no lane
# divergence.
void f(Vector[int] xs):
    unsafe:
        xs.pop()
    print(xs.len())

void main():
    Vector[int] a = [1, 2, 3, 4]
    f(a)
    print(a.len())
